From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] render: don't hand a NULL texture to the thumbnail render pass

view_render_to_buffer_iterator() guards on wlr_surface_has_buffer() and then
passes wlr_surface_get_texture() straight into wlr_render_pass_add_texture()
without checking it. Those are not the same condition: has_buffer() asks
whether the surface has a committed buffer, while get_texture() returns the
renderer's texture for that buffer, which is a separate object and can be NULL
even when a buffer is committed.

When it is NULL the render pass dereferences it and phoc dies:

  #0  wlr_render_pass_add_texture
  #1  view_render_to_buffer_iterator
  #2  surface_for_each_surface
  #3  thumbnail_frame_handle_copy
      libffi -> libwayland-server -> wl_event_loop_dispatch
  #9  wayland_event_source_dispatch    src/server.c:171

Reproduced on a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, Adreno 540, mainline 6.18) by driving
Firefox until the GPU faults. The A540 hits a fault, the msm driver runs
hangcheck recovery and resets the GPU, and shortly afterwards phosh asks for a
window thumbnail -- opening the on-screen keyboard is enough, since the
re-layout drives a screencopy. The texture has not survived the reset, and
phoc segfaults, which takes the whole session down and looks to the user like
the phone rebooting.

The neighbouring output render path already gets this right; render_surface_
iterator() in the same file does:

	struct wlr_texture *texture = wlr_surface_get_texture (surface);
	if (!texture)
		return;

so make the thumbnail path agree with it. A surface whose texture is gone is
simply skipped, the thumbnail comes out missing that surface, and the
compositor stays up.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 src/render.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/render.c b/src/render.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/render.c
+++ b/src/render.c
@@ -413,6 +413,9 @@ view_render_to_buffer_iterator (struct wlr_surface *surface, int sx, int sy, voi
     return;

   texture = wlr_surface_get_texture (surface);
+  if (!texture)
+    return;
+
   phoc_view_get_geometry (data->view, &geo);
   wlr_surface_get_buffer_source_box (surface, &src_box);

--
